    <dl>
      <dt>Resort type</dt><dd>Deluxe Villa resort at Disney's Wilderness Lodge, in the Magic Kingdom Resort Area. Disney Vacation Club inventory is mixed with cash bookings.</dd>
      <dt>Address</dt><dd>901 Timberline Drive, Lake Buena Vista, FL 32830 (same campus as Wilderness Lodge; confirm check-in location on your reservation)</dd>
      <dt>Size</dt><dd>Villas in a wing of the Wilderness Lodge grounds, styled after the railroad era of the American West. The property is shared with the lodge hotel and Copper Creek Villas &amp; Cabins.</dd>
      <dt>Rooms</dt><dd>Deluxe Studios sleep 5; one-bedroom villas sleep 4; two-bedroom villas sleep 8. A single child under 3 in a crib does not count toward the maximum. There is no Grand Villa category in the 2026 cash-rate table we used.</dd>
      <dt>Beds</dt><dd>Studio: 1 queen, 1 queen-size pull-down (or sleeper sofa) and 1 single pull-down. One-bedroom: 1 king and 1 queen-size pull-down or sleeper sofa. Two-bedroom: 1 king, 2 queens and 1 queen-size pull-down or sleeper sofa.</dd>
      <dt>Getting around</dt><dd>Boat to Magic Kingdom; boats also connect to the Contemporary and Fort Wilderness. Buses to EPCOT, Hollywood Studios, Animal Kingdom, the water parks and Disney Springs</dd>
      <dt>Food</dt><dd>Whispering Canyon Cafe, Story Book Dining at Artist Point, Roaring Fork and Geyser Point Bar &amp; Grill, shared with the lodge</dd>
      <dt>Pools</dt><dd>Boulder Ridge Cove Pool (quieter, zero-entry) and Copper Creek Springs Pool (main pool, with a 67-foot slide)</dd>
