  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Boulder Ridge is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families who need a fifth bed in a studio</strong> and want to stay at Wilderness Lodge. Official 2026 listings put Boulder Ridge studios at five adults; Copper Creek studios are listed at four.</li>
      <li><strong>People who want a quieter wing and the Cove Pool,</strong> while still using the lodge boat and restaurants.</li>
      <li><strong>Groups who do not need a Grand Villa or a cabin.</strong> This building's 2026 cash categories stop at a two-bedroom villa.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You need a fifth bed in a one-bedroom.</strong> Official listings cap the one-bedroom at four adults.</li>
      <li><strong>You wanted a Copper Creek cabin or a Grand Villa.</strong> Those are on the Copper Creek page, not here.</li>
      <li><strong>A monorail from the building is the main draw.</strong> This is a boat to Magic Kingdom, plus a walk from some villas to the dock.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: who you think this resort is really for, from your own stays. Two or three sentences.]</span>
  </section>

  <section id="rooms">
    <h2>Room types, sizes and beds</h2>
    <p>This guide covers Boulder Ridge Villas. The hotel rooms at <a href="/resorts/wilderness-lodge-resort/">Wilderness Lodge</a> and the villas and cabins at <a href="/resorts/copper-creek-villas-resort/">Copper Creek</a> have their own pages. Guests share restaurants, the boat dock and both pools. Official 2026 bed notes list a pull-down or a sleeper sofa in some rooms. Studios typically have a kitchenette; one-bedroom villas and larger typically have a full kitchen <span class="verify">[verify current appliances]</span>. There is no extra-adult charge up to the occupancy limit.</p>
