  <section id="dining">
    <h2>Dining</h2>
    <p>There is no separate Boulder Ridge restaurant. Guests use the lodge dining rooms: Whispering Canyon Cafe (brunch and dinner skillets), Story Book Dining at Artist Point, Roaring Fork and Geyser Point Bar &amp; Grill. Hours we last checked are on the <a href="/resorts/wilderness-lodge-resort/">Wilderness Lodge guide</a>. <span class="verify">[verify hours still current]</span></p>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: your go-to meal here, and one thing you'd skip.]</span>
  </section>

  <section id="pools">
    <h2>Pools and things to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Boulder Ridge Cove Pool</strong> is the quieter zero-entry pool at this wing, with a whirlpool spa. Lodge and Copper Creek guests can use it too.</li>
      <li><strong>Copper Creek Springs Pool</strong> is the main pool, with a 67-foot slide built into the rocks, hot and cold whirlpool spas, and a children's play area. Geyser Point is next to it.</li>
    </ul>
